Package: odrlITR
Type: Package
Title: Orthogonal Double Residual Learning for Individualized Treatment Rules
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jiaqi", "Tong", email = "jiaqi.tong@yale.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-8922-3386")),
    person("Fan", "Li", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Learns individualized treatment rules with the orthogonal double
    residual loss. First-stage propensity and marginal outcome regressions may
    be estimated by cross-fitted Super Learner, cross-fitted parametric models,
    or supplied directly by the user. The second stage supports exact
    optimization over linear rules and shallow decision trees, as well as
    hinge, exponential, logistic, squared-hinge, and custom surrogate-loss
    relaxations over reproducing-kernel Hilbert-space and neural-network score
    classes. The nuisance, policy, tuning, and prediction interfaces are
    modular and auditable.
